        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 5 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"id\", \"income_k\", \"age_years\", \"gender_code\", \n\"mood\"), Documented = c(\"no\", \"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\"), Label = c(NA, \nNA, \"Age in years\", \"Gender of the participant\", \"Positive affect\"\n), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA, NA, \"age\", \"gender\", \"mood\"), \n    Source = c(NA, NA, \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\"\n    ), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \"unlabelled\", \"llm\", \"llm\", \"labelled\"\n    )), row.names = c(NA, 5L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Documented but Unused Variables\n\n2 documented variables were not matched to any data column.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Variable = c(\"participant_id\", \"income_thousands\"\n), Label = c(\"Participant number\", \"Income in thousands\"), Source = c(\"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\")), row.names = c(1L, 4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "LLM model 'mock/rv' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 0 files, matched 2 columns, merged 0 labels)."
